{"title":"2013 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There is at least one Friday the Thirteenth in every year.\n</p><p>(a) What is the latest possible month in which the first Friday the Thirteenth can occur?\n</p><p>(b) In a year in which the first Friday the Thirteenth occurs in its latest month, what day of the week is January <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p>The table below shows the number of days in each month. February has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/5/0657f5cd42256c0a39d45b265235e2a939625515.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$29$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> days in leap years and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/6/9265f5dd6dade78136a6be158ace46bf7c0f8ce3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$28$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> in others.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57eb43dea04c8026018bcc8e92a9c206c78e44fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\begin{tabular}{|c|c|c|c|c|c|c|c|c|c|c|c|} \\hline JAN &amp; FEB &amp; MAR &amp; APR &amp; MAY &amp; JUN &amp; JUL &amp; AUG &amp; SEP &amp; OCT &amp; NOV &amp; DEC \\\\ \\hline 31 &amp; 28 or 29 &amp; 31 &amp; 30 &amp; 31 &amp; 30 &amp; 31 &amp; 31 &amp; 30 &amp; 31 &amp; 30 &amp; 31 \\\\ \\hline \\end{tabular}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"691\" height=\"42\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<pre>(a) OCTOBER (b) SATURDAY\n</pre>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_UNCO_Math_Contest_II\" title=\"2013 UNCO Math Contest II\">2013 UNCO Math Contest II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems\" title=\"2013 UNCO Math Contest II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2013 UNCO Math Contest II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://uncmathcontest.wordpress.com/\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2013 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2013 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_1